re-flop), leading out with a bet is risky. Your hand has showdown value as high cards, but it is safer to control the pot size.\n\nReason: Checking is the most prudent play here to minimize risk while retaining the potential to hit a King or Queen on later streets. It avoids bloating the pot with a marginal hand out of position.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
